const conceptCards = [{"id":"cq3-01","m":1,"t":"Q3.1 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释描述性、预测性和规范性建模的目标","h":"Explain the objectives of descriptive, predictive, and prescriptive modeling.","a":"中文：描述性建模总结过去发生了什么；预测性建模估计未来或未见数据会发生什么；规范性建模比较可选行动并帮助决定应该做什么。\n\nEnglish: Descriptive modeling explains what happened. Predictive modeling estimates what may happen on new data. Prescriptive modeling compares actions and helps decide what to do.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.1"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-02","m":1,"t":"Q3.2 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释有监督学习与无监督学习的两个区别","h":"Explain two differences between supervised and unsupervised learning.","a":"中文：有监督学习有目标变量，主要用于预测；无监督学习没有目标变量，主要发现结构或分组。有监督学习可用测试误差或交叉验证客观评价，无监督学习的评价通常更主观。\n\nEnglish: Supervised learning has a target and focuses on prediction. Unsupervised learning has no target and looks for structure. Supervised results can be checked with validation error, while unsupervised results are harder to evaluate objectively.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.2"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-03","m":1,"t":"Q3.3 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释回归问题与分类问题的主要区别","h":"Explain the main difference between regression and classification problems.","a":"中文：回归预测数值型目标，如损失金额；分类预测类别型目标，如是否理赔。两者使用的损失函数和评价指标也不同。\n\nEnglish: Regression predicts a numeric target, while classification predicts a categorical target. They therefore use different loss functions and performance measures.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.3"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-04","m":1,"t":"Q3.4 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释预测建模问题的三个特点","h":"Explain three characteristics of predictive modeling problems.","a":"中文：需要明确的目标变量和可用的预测变量；模型必须能应用到未来或未见数据；模型质量应使用与业务目标一致的指标在样本外评价。\n\nEnglish: A predictive problem needs a clear target and available predictors. The model must work on future or unseen data. Its performance should be measured out of sample with a metric linked to the business goal.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.4"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-05","m":1,"t":"Q3.5 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 KPI 的两个理想特点","h":"Explain two desirable characteristics of a key performance indicator.","a":"中文：KPI 应与业务目标直接相关，能反映真正重要的结果；同时应定义清楚、可量化并能用可靠数据持续计算，从而支持行动和比较。\n\nEnglish: A KPI should be closely linked to the business goal. It should also be clearly defined, measurable with reliable data, and useful for making decisions.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.5"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-06","m":2,"t":"Q3.6 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释分层抽样如何工作及其为何更具代表性","h":"Explain how stratified sampling works and why it can be more representative than random sampling.","a":"中文：先按重要变量把总体分成若干层，再从每一层随机抽样，最后合并。这样能保证小群体或关键群体进入样本，减少简单随机抽样偶然漏掉某些群体的风险。\n\nEnglish: Divide the population into important groups, take a random sample from each group, and combine the samples. This keeps small or important groups represented and can be more representative than a simple random sample.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.6"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-07","m":2,"t":"Q3.7 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释实践中应检查的三个数据质量问题","h":"Explain three data quality issues to examine in practice.","a":"中文：检查缺失值是否大量存在或具有系统性；检查不可能值、录入错误和异常值；检查变量定义、单位、类别编码和不同数据源是否一致。还应留意重复记录与过时数据。\n\nEnglish: Check missing values and whether they follow a pattern. Check impossible values, errors, and outliers. Also check whether definitions, units, category codes, and data sources are consistent.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.7"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-08","m":2,"t":"Q3.8 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 proxy variable 及其潜在问题","h":"Explain what a proxy variable is and why it may be problematic.","a":"中文：proxy variable 是与某个不可直接使用的属性高度相关、因而间接代表该属性的变量。它可能造成不公平或歧视，并让模型使用业务上不应使用的信息；即使删除敏感变量，proxy 仍可能保留其影响。\n\nEnglish: A proxy variable indirectly represents another attribute because they are strongly related. It can create unfair or discriminatory predictions and may keep the effect of a sensitive variable even after that variable is removed.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.8"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-09","m":2,"t":"Q3.9 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 target leakage 的问题","h":"Explain the problem with target leakage in predictive analytics.","a":"中文：target leakage 是特征使用了预测时不会得到的信息，或直接、间接包含目标结果。模型验证会显得异常优秀，但部署后无法取得这些信息，因此真实表现会大幅下降。\n\nEnglish: Target leakage occurs when a feature uses information that is unavailable at prediction time or reveals the target. Validation then looks too good, but real future performance will be poor.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.9"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-10","m":2,"t":"Q3.10 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释如何按时间划分训练集与测试集及其优势","h":"Explain how to use time for a training-test split and its advantage.","a":"中文：用较早时期的数据训练，用较晚时期的数据测试，并确保训练记录在测试记录之前。这样更接近真实部署过程，并能检验模型能否应对时间趋势和数据漂移。\n\nEnglish: Train on earlier observations and test on later observations. This matches real deployment and shows whether the model can handle time trends and data drift.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.10"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-11","m":1,"t":"Q3.11 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 loss function 的作用","h":"Explain what a loss function does.","a":"中文：损失函数把预测与实际结果之间的差异变成一个数值。模型拟合通过最小化总损失来选择参数，不同损失函数代表对不同类型错误的不同重视程度。\n\nEnglish: A loss function assigns a cost to the difference between a prediction and the actual result. Model fitting chooses parameters that minimize total loss, and different losses place different weight on errors.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.11"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-12","m":1,"t":"Q3.12 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 MAE 相对 MSE 的优点与缺点","h":"Explain the advantages and disadvantages of MAE over MSE.","a":"中文：MAE 使用绝对误差，对极端值不如 MSE 敏感，且与目标变量单位相同、容易解释。缺点是它在 0 处不可微，优化可能更困难，而且不会像 MSE 那样特别惩罚大误差。\n\nEnglish: MAE is less sensitive to outliers and is easy to interpret in the target's units. However, it is not differentiable at zero and does not give very large errors the strong penalty used by MSE.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.12"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-13","m":1,"t":"Q3.13 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 hyperparameter 及其重要性","h":"Explain what hyperparameters are and why they are important.","a":"中文：超参数不是由单次模型拟合直接估计的参数，而是在拟合前设定的模型控制值，如树深、正则化强度或邻居数。它们控制模型复杂度和偏差-方差权衡，因此会显著影响样本外表现。\n\nEnglish: Hyperparameters are model settings chosen before fitting, such as tree depth or penalty strength. They control model complexity and the bias-variance trade-off, so they strongly affect performance on new data.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.13"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-14","m":1,"t":"Q3.14 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释交叉验证及其如何调节超参数","h":"Explain how cross-validation works and how it tunes hyperparameters.","a":"中文：把训练数据分成 K 折，每次用 K-1 折拟合、剩余一折验证，轮流重复并平均误差。对每组超参数重复此过程，选择平均验证误差最低或符合 one-standard-error rule 的组合。\n\nEnglish: Split the training data into K folds. Fit on K-1 folds and validate on the remaining fold, rotating through all folds. Repeat for each hyperparameter choice and select the best mean validation result.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.14"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-15","m":1,"t":"Q3.15 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释预测分析中的 bias 与 variance","h":"Explain the difference between bias and variance.","a":"中文：bias 是模型因过于简单或假设错误而产生的系统性误差；variance 是模型对训练样本变化的敏感程度。复杂模型通常降低 bias 但提高 variance，应选择使测试误差最低的平衡点。\n\nEnglish: Bias is systematic error from an overly simple model or wrong assumptions. Variance is sensitivity to changes in the training sample. More complexity often lowers bias but raises variance.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.15"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-16","m":1,"t":"Q3.16 · Chapter 3 review","q":"描述欠拟合与过拟合模型的典型特点","h":"Describe the typical characteristics of underfitted and overfitted models.","a":"中文：欠拟合模型过于简单，在训练集和测试集上的误差都高，通常表现为高 bias、低 variance。过拟合模型训练误差很低但测试误差较高，学习了训练噪声，通常是低 bias、高 variance。\n\nEnglish: An underfitted model is too simple and has high error on both training and test data. An overfitted model has very low training error but much higher test error because it learns noise.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.16"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-17","m":3,"t":"Q3.17 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 variable 与 feature 的区别","h":"Explain the difference between variables and features.","a":"中文：variable 通常指原始数据中的字段；feature 指实际输入模型的变量，可以是原始变量，也可以由一个或多个原始变量转换、组合而成。\n\nEnglish: A variable is usually a field in the original data. A feature is an input used by the model and may be an original variable or a value created from other variables.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.17"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-18","m":3,"t":"Q3.18 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 feature generation 的两个用途","h":"Explain two uses of feature generation even when no new information is added.","a":"中文：第一，把原始信息转换成模型更容易捕捉的形式，例如对数、分箱或多项式项，以表示非线性。第二，组合变量形成更有业务意义或能表达交互的特征，从而改善预测或解释。\n\nEnglish: Feature generation can express an existing pattern in a form the model can use, such as a log or polynomial term. It can also combine variables to represent a business concept or an interaction more clearly.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.18"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-19","m":3,"t":"Q3.19 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 dimensionality 与 granularity 的两个区别","h":"Explain two differences between dimensionality and granularity.","a":"中文：dimensionality 指数据中变量或特征的数量；granularity 指一个变量或记录表示信息的细致程度。增加特征会提高维度，而把地区细分到邮编、把年份细分到月份会提高粒度，并可能产生稀疏类别。\n\nEnglish: Dimensionality is the number of variables or features. Granularity is the level of detail within a variable or observation. More columns increase dimension, while finer groups or time units increase granularity.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.19"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-20","m":4,"t":"Q3.20 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 RSS 和 R squared 作为模型选择指标的问题","h":"Explain the problem with RSS and R squared as model selection measures.","a":"中文：加入预测变量不会增大训练 RSS，也不会降低训练 R squared，因此这两个指标总偏向更复杂的模型。它们不惩罚复杂度，不能可靠反映样本外表现。\n\nEnglish: Adding predictors cannot increase training RSS or decrease training R squared. These measures therefore favor larger models and do not protect against overfitting.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.20"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-21","m":4,"t":"Q3.21 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释为何 AIC 和 BIC 是预测表现的间接指标","h":"Explain why AIC and BIC are indirect measures of prediction performance.","a":"中文：AIC 和 BIC 根据训练数据的似然或 RSS，再加上复杂度惩罚来估计模型质量。它们没有直接在未见数据上计算预测误差，因此只是样本外表现的理论近似。\n\nEnglish: AIC and BIC combine in-sample fit with a complexity penalty. They estimate expected model quality but do not directly measure prediction error on unseen data.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.21"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-22","m":4,"t":"Q3.22 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 AIC 与 BIC 的原理和差异","h":"Explain the rationale behind and the difference between AIC and BIC.","a":"中文：两者都用复杂度惩罚抵消增加变量带来的训练拟合改善，数值越低越好。AIC 每个参数的惩罚约为 2；BIC 使用 log(n)，当样本量较大时惩罚更强，通常选择更简单的模型。\n\nEnglish: Both criteria reward fit and penalize the number of parameters. AIC uses a penalty of about 2 per parameter, while BIC uses log(n) and usually favors a simpler model when the sample is large.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.22"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-23","m":4,"t":"Q3.23 · Chapter 3 review","q":"描述线性模型假设成立时残差的性质","h":"Describe the residual properties when linear-model assumptions hold.","a":"中文：残差应以 0 为中心，相互独立，并在各拟合值下具有大致恒定的方差；对正态线性模型，还应近似正态。残差图中不应出现曲线、漏斗形或其他系统模式。\n\nEnglish: Residuals should be centered at zero, independent, and have roughly constant variance. For a normal linear model, they should also be approximately normal and show no clear pattern.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.23"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-24","m":4,"t":"Q3.24 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释多项式回归的优点和缺点","h":"Explain the advantages and disadvantages of polynomial regression.","a":"中文：优点是能用普通线性模型框架表示平滑非线性关系，拟合和预测较方便。缺点是次数需要调节，高次模型方差大、解释困难，并可能在数据边界或外推时产生不合理结果。\n\nEnglish: Polynomial regression captures smooth non-linear patterns while keeping a linear-model fitting framework. However, high degrees can overfit, are hard to explain, and may behave badly near boundaries or during extrapolation.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.24"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-25","m":4,"t":"Q3.25 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释线性模型如何处理分类预测变量","h":"Explain how categorical predictors are handled by a linear model.","a":"中文：选择一个类别作为 reference level，对其余 k-1 个类别建立 0/1 dummy variables。每个系数表示该类别相对于 reference level 的差异，并控制其他变量不变。\n\nEnglish: Choose one category as the reference and create k-1 indicator variables. Each coefficient compares one level with the reference level, holding other predictors constant.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.25"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-26","m":4,"t":"Q3.26 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 interaction 的含义","h":"Explain the meaning of interaction.","a":"中文：交互表示一个预测变量对目标的影响取决于另一个变量的取值。模型通常加入乘积项；此时主效应是在另一个变量等于 0 或处于 reference level 时的条件效应。\n\nEnglish: An interaction means that the effect of one predictor depends on another predictor. A product term allows different slopes or effects across values or groups.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.26"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-27","m":4,"t":"Q3.27 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释线性模型中共线变量的问题","h":"Explain the problems with collinear variables in a linear model.","a":"中文：高度相关的预测变量提供重复信息，使单个系数难以区分。系数会变得不稳定、标准误增大，符号和显著性可能随样本变化；预测可能仍可接受，但解释性明显下降。\n\nEnglish: Collinear predictors contain overlapping information. Their coefficients become unstable, standard errors grow, and signs or p-values may change across samples. Prediction may remain useful, but interpretation becomes difficult.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.27"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-28","m":4,"t":"Q3.28 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 best subset selection 及其局限","h":"Explain how best subset selection works and its limitations.","a":"中文：它拟合所有可能的预测变量子集，在每个模型大小中找最佳模型，再用 AIC、BIC 或验证误差选择。因为需要检查约 2^p 个模型，变量较多时计算量巨大，也可能因搜索过多而过拟合或选择不稳定。\n\nEnglish: Best subset selection fits every possible predictor subset and selects among them with a model criterion. It requires about 2^p models, so it becomes very expensive and may give unstable choices when p is large.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.28"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-29","m":4,"t":"Q3.29 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 stepwise selection 及其如何解决 best subset 的局限","h":"Explain how stepwise selection works and how it addresses best subset limitations.","a":"中文：stepwise 每一步只加入或删除一个变量，并在当前候选中选择改善最大的操作，直到不能继续改善。它只考察一条较小的模型路径，计算远少于所有子集；代价是贪心搜索可能错过全局最佳模型。\n\nEnglish: Stepwise selection adds or removes one predictor at a time and keeps the best move at each step. It fits far fewer models than best subset selection, but its greedy path may miss the best overall subset.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.29"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-30","m":4,"t":"Q3.30 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释为何 stepwise selection 不应一次加入或删除多个特征","h":"Explain why multiple features should not be added or dropped at one step.","a":"中文：一次改变多个变量会快速增加候选组合数量，削弱 stepwise 的计算优势，也难以判断改善来自哪个变量。逐个改变能清楚评价每个变量的增量贡献并保持搜索过程简单。\n\nEnglish: Changing several features at once creates many candidate combinations and removes the main efficiency benefit of stepwise selection. It also becomes hard to identify the incremental value of each feature.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.30"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-31","m":4,"t":"Q3.31 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 forward 与 backward stepwise selection 的两个区别","h":"Explain two differences between forward and backward stepwise selection.","a":"中文：forward 从空模型开始逐个加入变量；backward 从全模型开始逐个删除变量。forward 可在预测变量数大于样本量时使用，而 backward 必须先能拟合全模型；两条搜索路径可能得到不同结果。\n\nEnglish: Forward selection starts with no predictors and adds them. Backward selection starts with the full model and removes them. Forward can work when the full model cannot be fit, and the two paths may select different models.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.31"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-32","m":4,"t":"Q3.32 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 regularization 如何工作","h":"Explain how regularization works.","a":"中文：正则化在原损失函数上增加系数大小的惩罚，拟合时同时追求好拟合和小系数。它把系数向 0 收缩，以增加一些 bias 换取较低 variance，通常改善新数据表现。\n\nEnglish: Regularization adds a penalty for large coefficients to the loss function. It shrinks coefficients toward zero, adding some bias but reducing variance and often improving test performance.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.32"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-33","m":4,"t":"Q3.33 · Chapter 3 review","q":"描述拟合正则化回归前对变量的重要处理","h":"Describe an important modification before fitting regularized regression.","a":"中文：应先标准化数值预测变量，使其通常具有均值 0、标准差 1。否则惩罚大小会受变量单位影响，不同尺度的变量无法被公平收缩；截距通常不参与惩罚。\n\nEnglish: Standardize numeric predictors before fitting, usually to mean zero and standard deviation one. Otherwise, the penalty depends on the units of each predictor and does not treat them fairly.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.33"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-34","m":4,"t":"Q3.34 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 lambda 如何影响正则化模型","h":"Explain how lambda affects a regularized model.","a":"中文：lambda=0 时没有惩罚，得到未正则化模型。lambda 越大，收缩越强、模型越简单、bias 越高而 variance 越低；在 lasso 或 elastic net 中，更多系数可能变为 0。\n\nEnglish: At lambda=0, there is no penalty. A larger lambda gives stronger shrinkage, a simpler model, higher bias, and lower variance. With lasso-type penalties, more coefficients may become zero.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.34"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-35","m":4,"t":"Q3.35 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释为何 lambda 与 alpha 是超参数以及如何选择","h":"Explain why lambda and alpha are hyperparameters and how they are selected.","a":"中文：lambda 控制惩罚强度，alpha 控制 ridge 与 lasso 惩罚的混合；它们不是普通模型系数，不能由一次拟合直接决定。通常在训练数据上对 alpha-lambda 网格做交叉验证，选择验证误差最佳的组合。\n\nEnglish: Lambda controls penalty strength, and alpha controls the ridge-lasso mix. They are model settings rather than fitted coefficients, so they are usually selected by cross-validation over a grid.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.35"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-36","m":4,"t":"Q3.36 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 stepwise selection 与 regularization 的两个区别","h":"Explain two differences between stepwise selection and regularization.","a":"中文：stepwise 通过离散地加入或删除变量来选择子集，保留变量的系数通常不收缩；regularization 同时连续收缩所有系数，lasso 才可能把部分系数压到 0。正则化通常对相关变量和样本变化更稳定，但会引入偏差。\n\nEnglish: Stepwise selection adds or removes predictors and usually refits retained coefficients without shrinkage. Regularization continuously shrinks coefficients; lasso may set some to zero. Regularization is often more stable but introduces bias.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.36"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq3-37","m":4,"t":"Q3.37 · Chapter 3 review","q":"解释 elastic net 选择 lambda 的 one-standard-error rule","h":"Explain the one-standard-error rule for selecting lambda in an elastic net.","a":"中文：先找平均交叉验证误差最小的 lambda，再计算该最小误差的一个标准误范围。在误差不超过该范围的 lambda 中选择最大的 lambda，即选择惩罚更强、模型更简单但表现仍接近最佳的方案。\n\nEnglish: First find the lambda with the lowest mean cross-validation error. Then choose the largest lambda whose error is within one standard error of that minimum. This gives a simpler, more regularized model with nearly the same performance.","k":["Chapter 3","conceptual review","Q3.37"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-01","m":4,"t":"Q4.1 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 GLM 从哪两个方面推广了线性模型","h":"Explain the two ways in which a GLM generalizes a linear model.","a":"中文：第一，响应变量不必服从正态分布，而可以使用指数族中的分布，如二项、泊松、伽马或 Tweedie 分布。第二，响应变量的均值不必直接等于线性预测量，而是通过连接函数与线性预测量相连。\n\nEnglish: A GLM allows the response to follow a non-normal distribution from the exponential family. It also uses a link function to connect the mean response to the linear predictor.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.1"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-02","m":4,"t":"Q4.2 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释为什么线性模型是广义线性模型的特例","h":"Explain why a linear model is a special case of a generalized linear model.","a":"中文：普通线性模型使用正态响应分布和恒等连接函数。因此，它满足 GLM 的一般结构，只是分布和连接函数取了最简单的组合。\n\nEnglish: A linear model is a GLM with a normal response distribution and the identity link. Therefore, it is one special choice within the GLM framework.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.2"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-03","m":4,"t":"Q4.3 · Chapter 4 review","q":"描述 Tweedie 分布的特点","h":"Describe the characteristics of the Tweedie distribution.","a":"中文：当幂参数在 1 和 2 之间时，Tweedie 分布在 0 处有正概率，同时正值部分是连续且右偏的。它可看作复合泊松-伽马分布，适合大量为 0、其余为正连续值的总损失数据，并满足方差与均值幂次成比例的关系。\n\nEnglish: For a power parameter between 1 and 2, the Tweedie distribution has a positive mass at zero and a continuous, right-skewed positive part. It is a compound Poisson-gamma model and is useful for aggregate losses with many zeros.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.3"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-04","m":4,"t":"Q4.4 · Chapter 4 review","q":"当目标变量含有 0 时能否使用 log link","h":"Explain whether the log link can be used when some target observations are zero.","a":"中文：可以。log link 作用于条件均值而不是直接对观测值取对数，所以观测值可以为 0；模型只要求预测均值为正。这与先把响应变量变为 log(Y) 不同，后者无法直接处理 Y=0。\n\nEnglish: Yes. The log link is applied to the conditional mean, not to each observed response. The observations may be zero, while the fitted mean remains positive. This is different from modeling log(Y) directly.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.4"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-05","m":4,"t":"Q4.5 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 GLM 中 weight 与 offset 的两个区别","h":"Explain two differences between weights and offsets in a GLM.","a":"中文：weight 改变一条观测在模型拟合中的影响力，但不会进入预测公式，也没有估计系数。offset 是线性预测量的一部分，其系数固定为 1，因此会直接影响预测值，常用于已知的 exposure 效应。\n\nEnglish: A weight changes how much an observation affects model fitting, but it is not part of the prediction formula. An offset enters the linear predictor with a coefficient fixed at 1 and directly changes the prediction.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.5"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-06","m":4,"t":"Q4.6 · Chapter 4 review","q":"说明通常如何估计 GLM 参数","h":"State the statistical method typically used to estimate GLM parameters.","a":"中文：通常使用最大似然估计，选择使观测数据的似然函数最大的参数值。实际计算一般通过迭代算法完成。\n\nEnglish: GLM parameters are usually estimated by maximum likelihood. An iterative algorithm finds the parameter values that maximize the likelihood of the observed data.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.6"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-07","m":4,"t":"Q4.7 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释用 deviance 选择模型的问题","h":"Explain the problem with deviance as a model selection criterion.","a":"中文：加入更多预测变量通常只会降低或保持 deviance，因此单看 deviance 会偏向更复杂的模型。它没有对模型复杂度进行惩罚，容易导致过拟合。\n\nEnglish: Deviance usually decreases when more predictors are added. Because it has no penalty for model complexity, using deviance alone tends to select an overly complex model and may cause overfitting.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.7"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-08","m":4,"t":"Q4.8 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 likelihood ratio test 用于模型选择的局限","h":"Explain the limitations of the likelihood ratio test as a model selection method.","a":"中文：似然比检验只能直接比较嵌套模型，并依赖大样本近似和正确的分布假设。它一次只回答两个模型之间是否有显著改善，不能直接衡量新数据上的预测效果；反复检验还会增加错误选择的风险。\n\nEnglish: The likelihood ratio test directly compares only nested models and relies on distributional and large-sample assumptions. It does not directly measure prediction on new data, and repeated tests can lead to unstable choices.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.8"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-09","m":4,"t":"Q4.9 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 GLM 正则化如何工作","h":"Explain how regularization for GLMs works.","a":"中文：在 GLM 的负对数似然或 deviance 上加入系数惩罚项。惩罚会把系数向 0 收缩，以增加少量偏差换取较低方差。Ridge、lasso 和 elastic net 使用不同形式的惩罚，惩罚强度通常通过交叉验证选择。\n\nEnglish: Regularization adds a penalty for large coefficients to the GLM loss. It shrinks coefficients toward zero, trading some bias for lower variance. The penalty type and strength are usually selected by cross-validation.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.9"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-10","m":5,"t":"Q4.10 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释为什么二元分类器需要 cutoff","h":"Explain the importance of setting a cutoff for a binary classifier.","a":"中文：模型输出的是事件概率，cutoff 把概率转换为类别。不同 cutoff 会产生不同的假阳性与假阴性，因此应根据业务成本以及 sensitivity、specificity 等指标选择，而不是机械地使用 0.5。\n\nEnglish: A binary model produces probabilities, and the cutoff converts them into class predictions. The cutoff controls the balance between false positives and false negatives, so it should reflect business costs rather than always being 0.5.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.10"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-11","m":5,"t":"Q4.11 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 accuracy、sensitivity 与 specificity 的关系","h":"Explain the relationship between accuracy, sensitivity, and specificity.","a":"中文：sensitivity 是实际正类中被正确识别的比例，specificity 是实际负类中被正确识别的比例。accuracy 是两者按正负类占比加权后的平均：accuracy = prevalence × sensitivity + (1-prevalence) × specificity。\n\nEnglish: Sensitivity is the correct rate among actual positives, while specificity is the correct rate among actual negatives. Accuracy is their prevalence-weighted average.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.11"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-12","m":5,"t":"Q4.12 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 cutoff 如何影响 sensitivity 与 specificity","h":"Explain how the cutoff affects sensitivity and specificity.","a":"中文：降低 cutoff 会预测更多正类，通常提高 sensitivity、降低 specificity。提高 cutoff 会预测更少正类，通常降低 sensitivity、提高 specificity。\n\nEnglish: Lowering the cutoff creates more positive predictions, so sensitivity usually rises and specificity falls. Raising the cutoff usually has the opposite effect.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.12"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-13","m":2,"t":"Q4.13 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释不平衡数据的问题","h":"Explain the problem with unbalanced data.","a":"中文：当一个类别远多于另一个类别时，模型可能只擅长预测多数类，却仍得到很高的 accuracy。少数类通常才是业务关注对象，因此 accuracy 会产生误导，应同时检查 sensitivity、specificity、precision、AUC 或 PR 指标。\n\nEnglish: With unbalanced data, a model can obtain high accuracy by mainly predicting the majority class. Its performance on the important minority class may still be poor, so class-specific measures should also be reviewed.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.13"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-14","m":2,"t":"Q4.14 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释 undersampling 与 oversampling 如何平衡数据","h":"Explain how undersampling and oversampling make unbalanced data more balanced.","a":"中文：undersampling 从多数类中删除一部分记录；oversampling 重复或生成少数类记录。两种方法都改变训练数据中的类别比例，使模型更重视少数类。\n\nEnglish: Undersampling removes some majority-class records. Oversampling repeats or creates minority-class records. Both methods make the training classes more balanced.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.14"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-15","m":2,"t":"Q4.15 · Chapter 4 review","q":"解释为什么 oversampling 必须在训练测试划分之后进行","h":"Explain why oversampling must be performed after splitting the data.","a":"中文：如果先 oversample，再划分数据，同一条少数类记录的副本可能同时进入训练集和测试集，造成数据泄漏和过于乐观的测试结果。应先划分，再只对训练集 oversample，并保持测试集的真实类别比例。\n\nEnglish: If oversampling is done first, copies of the same record may appear in both training and test data. This causes leakage and an overly positive test result. Split first and oversample only the training data.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.15"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq4-16","m":2,"t":"Q4.16 · Chapter 4 review","q":"分别说明选择 oversampling 和 undersampling 的一个理由","h":"Give one reason for using oversampling over undersampling and one reason for the reverse.","a":"中文：当数据量不大或不想丢失多数类信息时，优先 oversampling；缺点是重复记录可能导致过拟合并增加计算量。当多数类数据非常多时，undersampling 更快且数据规模更小；缺点是会丢失信息。\n\nEnglish: Use oversampling when keeping all majority-class information is important, especially with a small dataset. Use undersampling when the majority class is very large and faster fitting is valuable, although some information is lost.","k":["Chapter 4","conceptual review","Q4.16"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-01","m":5,"t":"Q5.1 · Chapter 5 review","q":"简述决策树如何工作以及为何称为树模型","h":"Briefly explain how a decision tree works and why it is called a tree-based model.","a":"中文：决策树通过一系列 if-then 规则把特征空间反复分成更小区域，每个终端节点给出预测。其结构从根节点开始，经过分支到达叶节点，形状像倒置的树，因此称为树模型。\n\nEnglish: A decision tree repeatedly splits the feature space using if-then rules. Each terminal node gives a prediction. Its root, branches, and leaves form a tree-like structure.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.1"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-02","m":5,"t":"Q5.2 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释为什么分类错误率对节点不纯度不如 Gini 和 entropy 敏感","h":"Explain why classification error is less sensitive to node impurity than the Gini index and entropy.","a":"中文：分类错误率只取决于节点中的多数类别；只要多数类别不变，类别比例的小幅变化不会改变错误率。Gini 和 entropy 会随全部类别比例连续变化，因此更容易识别能改善节点纯度的划分。\n\nEnglish: Classification error depends only on the majority class. It may stay unchanged when class proportions change but the majority class does not. Gini and entropy respond smoothly to all class proportions and are more sensitive split measures.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.2"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-03","m":5,"t":"Q5.3 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 recursive binary splitting 中 top-down 和 greedy 的含义","h":"Explain the terms top-down and greedy in recursive binary splitting.","a":"中文：top-down 表示算法从包含全部数据的根节点开始，逐层向下划分。greedy 表示每一步只选择当前能最大降低不纯度或误差的划分，不会提前考虑该选择对后续划分的影响。\n\nEnglish: Top-down means starting with all observations at the root and splitting downward. Greedy means choosing the best split at the current step without considering later splits.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.3"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-04","m":5,"t":"Q5.4 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释为什么不应只在不纯度下降超过阈值时才继续生长树","h":"Explain why an impurity-reduction threshold is not a good rule for growing a tree.","a":"中文：某个当前划分的改善可能很小，但它可能为后续非常有价值的划分创造条件。过早使用阈值会错过这种结构。更好的方法是先生长一棵较大的树，再用剪枝和交叉验证控制复杂度。\n\nEnglish: A split with a small immediate gain may make a much better later split possible. A fixed threshold may stop the tree too early. It is better to grow a large tree and then prune it.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.4"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-05","m":5,"t":"Q5.5 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 cost-complexity pruning 如何工作","h":"Explain how cost-complexity pruning works.","a":"中文：先生长一棵较大的树，再考虑它的不同子树。评价标准把训练误差与终端节点数量的惩罚相加；复杂度参数越大，对大树的惩罚越强。最终用交叉验证选择合适参数和子树。\n\nEnglish: First grow a large tree and consider its possible subtrees. Cost-complexity pruning adds a penalty for the number of terminal nodes to the training error. Cross-validation selects the penalty and the final subtree.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.5"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-06","m":5,"t":"Q5.6 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 complexity parameter 如何影响决策树质量","h":"Explain how the complexity parameter affects the quality of a decision tree.","a":"中文：较小的复杂度参数允许更多划分，树更大、偏差较低但方差和过拟合风险较高。较大的参数产生较小的树，方差较低但可能欠拟合。应在两者之间寻找验证误差最低的位置。\n\nEnglish: A small complexity parameter allows a larger tree with lower bias but higher variance. A large value gives a smaller tree that may underfit. The best value balances these effects on validation data.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.6"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-07","m":5,"t":"Q5.7 · Chapter 5 review","q":"描述如何用交叉验证调整决策树的 complexity parameter","h":"Describe how to tune the complexity parameter using cross-validation.","a":"中文：在训练数据中为一组 complexity parameter 值做 K 折交叉验证，计算每个值的平均验证误差。可选择误差最小的值，或使用 one-standard-error rule，在误差仍可接受的范围内选择更简单的树。最后只在未使用的测试集上评估一次。\n\nEnglish: Use K-fold cross-validation on the training data for a grid of complexity values. Select the value with the lowest mean error, or use the one-standard-error rule to choose a simpler tree.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.7"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-08","m":5,"t":"Q5.8 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释决策树如何处理分类预测变量","h":"Explain how decision trees handle categorical predictors.","a":"中文：对一个具有多个水平的分类变量，树寻找一种把这些水平分成左右两组的方式，使不纯度或误差下降最多。它不要求类别之间有数值距离，但水平太多会产生大量候选划分并增加过拟合风险。\n\nEnglish: A tree divides the levels of a categorical predictor into two groups and chooses the grouping with the largest improvement. No numeric distance between levels is required, but many levels create many candidate splits.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.8"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-09","m":5,"t":"Q5.9 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释单调变换数值预测变量和目标变量对树的影响","h":"Explain how monotone transformations of a numeric predictor and the target affect a tree.","a":"中文：对数值预测变量做单调变换不会改变观测排序，因此树可以找到等价的切分，树结构和预测分组通常不变。对回归树的目标变量做单调变换会改变均值、平方误差和划分质量，所以树结构与预测都可能改变；预测还需要变换回原尺度。\n\nEnglish: A monotone transformation of a numeric predictor preserves its order, so equivalent splits and usually the same tree are obtained. Transforming a regression target changes means and squared errors, so it can change the splits and predictions.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.9"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-10","m":5,"t":"Q5.10 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释树为何偏好水平很多的分类变量及其问题","h":"Explain why a tree favors categorical predictors with many levels and the resulting problems.","a":"中文：水平越多，可尝试的分组越多，因此仅靠偶然性也更可能找到看似很好的划分。这会造成变量选择偏差、过拟合和不稳定的小节点；未来数据还可能出现未见水平。可考虑合并水平、降低粒度或限制节点大小。\n\nEnglish: A predictor with many levels offers many possible splits, so it has a greater chance of producing a strong split by luck. This causes selection bias, overfitting, small unstable nodes, and possible new levels in future data.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.10"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-11","m":5,"t":"Q5.11 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释随机森林如何工作","h":"Explain how a random forest works.","a":"中文：随机森林对多个 bootstrap 样本分别生长树，并在每个节点只从随机抽取的 mtry 个预测变量中寻找划分。最后平均回归预测或汇总分类预测。随机选变量使树之间相关性降低，平均后可显著降低方差。\n\nEnglish: A random forest grows many trees on bootstrap samples. At each split, it considers only a random subset of predictors. The trees are combined by averaging or voting, and the random feature step reduces correlation between trees.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.11"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-12","m":5,"t":"Q5.12 · Chapter 5 review","q":"描述分类随机森林汇总基树预测类别的两种方法","h":"Describe two ways a classification random forest can form its final predicted class.","a":"中文：第一种是 majority vote：每棵树投一个类别，票数最多的类别获胜。第二种是先平均各树给出的类别概率，再用 cutoff 或最大概率确定最终类别。\n\nEnglish: One method is majority voting across the tree predictions. Another is to average the class probabilities from the trees and then apply a cutoff or choose the largest probability.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.12"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-13","m":5,"t":"Q5.13 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释选择随机森林 mtry 参数时的考虑","h":"Explain the considerations in choosing the mtry parameter.","a":"中文：较大的 mtry 使每棵树更强，但树之间更相似；较小的 mtry 增强去相关效果，却可能让单棵树变弱。因此需在单树质量与树间相关性之间权衡，并用 OOB 误差或交叉验证调参。默认值只能作为起点。\n\nEnglish: A large mtry makes individual trees stronger but more correlated. A small value decorrelates the trees but may weaken each tree. Tune it with out-of-bag error or cross-validation.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.13"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-14","m":5,"t":"Q5.14 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 boosted tree 如何工作","h":"Explain how a boosted tree works.","a":"中文：boosting 按顺序建立许多小树。每棵新树重点拟合前面模型尚未解释好的误差或负梯度，并按 learning rate 缩小后加入现有模型。最终预测是所有树贡献的加总。\n\nEnglish: Boosting builds small trees in sequence. Each new tree focuses on the errors or negative gradients left by the current model. Its contribution is scaled by the learning rate and added to the ensemble.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.14"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-15","m":5,"t":"Q5.15 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释随机森林与 boosted tree 的相同点和不同点","h":"Explain the similarities and differences between a random forest and a boosted tree.","a":"中文：两者都组合多棵树，通常比单树预测更准确且更难解释。随机森林的树可并行建立，通过 bootstrap 和随机特征减少方差；boosting 的树按顺序建立，后面的树纠正前面的错误，常能降低偏差，但更依赖 learning rate、树深和树数的调节。\n\nEnglish: Both methods combine many trees and are usually more accurate than one tree. Random forest builds trees in parallel and mainly reduces variance. Boosting builds trees in sequence to correct earlier errors and often reduces bias.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.15"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-16","m":5,"t":"Q5.16 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释基树数量和 shrinkage 如何影响 boosted tree","h":"Explain how the number of trees and shrinkage affect a boosted tree.","a":"中文：更多基树让模型逐步学习更多结构，但树太多时可能过拟合。较小的 shrinkage 或 learning rate 降低每棵树的影响，通常需要更多树，却往往带来更稳定的泛化表现。这两个参数必须一起调节。\n\nEnglish: More trees let the model learn more structure, but too many may overfit. A smaller shrinkage value gives each tree less influence and usually requires more trees, often improving generalization. Tune both parameters together.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.16"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-17","m":5,"t":"Q5.17 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 variable importance score 如何计算","h":"Explain how variable importance scores are calculated.","a":"中文：常见的 split importance 把某变量在所有以它划分的节点上带来的不纯度或平方误差下降相加，再在全部树中平均并标准化。数值越大表示模型越依赖该变量，但不表示作用方向或因果关系。另一常见方法是打乱变量后观察预测误差增加多少。\n\nEnglish: Split importance adds the impurity or squared-error reduction from all splits using a variable, then averages and scales the result across trees. A permutation version measures how much prediction error rises after that variable is shuffled.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.17"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-18","m":5,"t":"Q5.18 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 PDP 以及它比 variable importance plot 改进之处","h":"Explain what a partial dependence plot is and how it improves on a variable importance plot.","a":"中文：PDP 依次把某特征设为一组网格值，对全部记录计算预测并取平均，展示平均预测如何随该特征变化。variable importance 只说明变量有多重要，而 PDP 还能显示效应的方向、形状和非线性。\n\nEnglish: A PDP sets one feature to each value on a grid, predicts all records, and averages the predictions. Unlike variable importance, it shows the direction and shape of the fitted relationship.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.18"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq5-19","m":5,"t":"Q5.19 · Chapter 5 review","q":"解释 PDP 的两个缺点","h":"Explain two drawbacks of a partial dependence plot.","a":"中文：第一，当预测变量高度相关时，PDP 会构造现实中很少出现甚至不可能出现的特征组合。第二，平均曲线可能掩盖个体差异和交互作用，即不同记录可能具有方向完全不同的效应。\n\nEnglish: First, correlated predictors can make a PDP use unrealistic feature combinations. Second, averaging can hide different individual patterns and interactions. The plot should therefore be interpreted with care.","k":["Chapter 5","conceptual review","Q5.19"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-01","m":3,"t":"Q6.1 · Unsupervised learning","q":"解释无监督学习为何通常比有监督学习更具挑战性（给出两点理由）","h":"Why is unsupervised learning usually more challenging than supervised learning? Give two reasons.","a":"中文：1. 目标更模糊（Less clearly defined objectives）：与有监督学习不同，无监督学习没有像\"预测\"这样简单清晰的目标，具体想达成什么往往更模糊、更主观。 2. 结果更难客观评估（Less objective evaluation）：有监督学习可以通过模型对目标变量的预测效果来检验，而无监督学习缺少目标变量，基于目标变量的评估方法（如交叉验证）不再适用，因此很难客观地评估所得结果的质量——\"No one is 'supervising' our work!\"\n\nEnglish: 1. *Less clearly defined objectives*: Unlike supervised learning, objectives in the unsupervised learning domain become more fuzzy and subjective because there is no simple goal like prediction. 2. *Less objective evaluation*: For supervised learning, we can check our work by seeing how well the model predicts the target variable. In contrast, a target variable is absent in unsupervised learning, so methods for assessing model quality based on the target variable (e.g., cross-validation) are generally not applicable, which makes it difficult to evaluate the results obtained. No one is \"supervising\" our work!","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.1"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-02","m":3,"t":"Q6.2 · PCA","q":"解释主成分分析（PCA）是如何工作的","h":"Explain how principal component analysis works.","a":"中文：PCA 是一种高级数据分析技术，它将高维数据集变换为一组数量更少、更易于处理的代表性变量（representative variables），即主成分（PCs）。这些 PCs 是原始变量的线性组合，能够共同简化数据集、降低其维度，并使其更便于数据探索和可视化。PCA 特别适合高度相关的数据——对于此类数据，少数几个 PC 就足以代表全数据集的大部分信息。\n\nEnglish: Principal components analysis (PCA) is an advanced data-analytic technique that transforms a high-dimensional dataset into a smaller, much more manageable set of representative variables (hence the qualifier \"principal,\" meaning major or representative). Known as principal components (PCs), these composite variables are linear combinations of the existing variables generated to collectively simplify the dataset, reducing its dimension and making it more amenable to data exploration and visualization. This technique especially lends itself to highly correlated data, for which a few PCs are enough to represent most of the information in the full dataset.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.2"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-03","m":3,"t":"Q6.3 · PCA uses","q":"解释主成分分析的两个常见用途","h":"Explain two common uses of principal component analysis.","a":"中文：1. 数据可视化（Data visualization）：通过 PCA，我们将 p 个变量压缩为 M 个 PCs，这些 PCs 共同保留了以方差衡量的绝大部分信息，然后可以在二维或三维图中直观展示样本结构。 2. 特征生成（Feature generation）：用 M 个互不相关的 PCs Z_1,\\dots,Z_M 替代原始的 p 个相关变量 X_1,\\dots,X_p，作为预测目标变量的预测变量。这些预测变量按构造就是互不相关的，因此一个变量被另一个变量的相关性所混淆的问题不复存在。通过降低数据维度和模型复杂度，我们希望优化偏差–方差权衡（bias–variance trade-off），从而提升模型的预测表现。\n\nEnglish: 1. *Data visualization*: Via PCA, we successfully reduce the dimension of the dataset from p variables to a smaller set of variables (more precisely, the M PCs) that together retain most of the information measured by variance. 2. *Feature generation*: Once we have settled on the number of PCs to use (typically, we will use just the first few), the original variables X_1,\\dots,X_p are replaced by the PCs Z_1,\\dots,Z_M, which capture most of the information in the dataset and serve as predictors for the target variable. These predictors are, by construction, mutually uncorrelated, so the effect of one variable being confounded by another variable due to their correlations is no longer an issue. By reducing the dimension of the data and the complexity of the model, we hope to optimize the bias–variance trade-off and improve the prediction performance of the model.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.3"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-04","m":3,"t":"Q6.4 · Scree plot","q":"解释如何使用碎石图（scree plot）来选择所要使用的主成分数量","h":"Explain how a scree plot is used to choose the number of principal components.","a":"中文：碎石图以主成分序号（1 到 p）为横轴、每个 PC 的方差解释比例（PVE）为纵轴。由于 PVE 随 PC 序号递减，我们通过\"目测\"碎石图，寻找后续 PCs 的 PVE 已下降到足够低水平的那个点——这个点称为碎石图中的\"elbow\"（肘部）。elbow 之前的 PCs 保留，elbow 之后的 PCs 的 PVE 可忽略不计，可以安全丢弃。不幸的是，这种视觉分析本质上是ad hoc（临时/目测法）的，定位 elbow 是相当主观的（多低才算低？），因此 PA 考试中只要你的选择用上述逻辑加以论证，通常会给出一个可接受的范围。\n\nEnglish: The PVEs provide a simple visual inspection method for selecting the number of PCs. We use a scree plot to display the PVEs of the PCs against the PC index in order (from 1 to p). As the PVE will decrease as we go to the later PCs and move along the horizontal axis of a scree plot, we will typically choose the smallest number of PCs required to explain a sizable proportion of variance. We can do so by \"eyeballing\" the scree plot and looking for the point at which the PVEs of subsequent PCs have dropped off to a sufficiently low level. We call that point an elbow in the scree plot. The PCs beyond the elbow have a negligible PVE and can be safely dropped without losing much information. Unfortunately, this type of visual analysis is inherently ad hoc, and locating the elbow can be a rather subjective exercise (how \"low\" is low?), so the model solution of a typical PA exam will likely have a range of acceptable values for the number of PCs to use. As long as you justify your choice with the reasoning above, you will be fine.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.4"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-05","m":3,"t":"Q6.5 · PCA scaling","q":"解释对变量进行中心化与缩放会如何影响主成分分析的结果","h":"Explain how centering and scaling affect PCA results.","a":"中文：中心化（Centering）：将变量减去其均值使其均值为 0，对 PC 载荷没有实质影响，因为方差在加减常数后不变（prcomp() 默认即做中心化）。 缩放（Scaling）：PCA 结果对变量量纲非常敏感——若按原尺度做 PCA，等价于基于变量间的协方差矩阵；若先标准化（标准差均为 1）再做 PCA，则等价于基于相关矩阵。两者得到的 PC 通常不同。因此，与 PCA 类似，我们通常在聚类分析前将变量缩放到标准差为 1，除非应用场景暗示某些变量应获得更高权重。\n\nEnglish: *Centering*: Subtracting the mean theoretically does not affect the loadings because variance is unchanged by an additive constant — prcomp() centers by default. *Scaling*: PCA results are highly sensitive to the scale on which the feature values are measured. PCA on the raw scale is based on the covariance matrix, while PCA on standardized variables (with unit standard deviation) is based on the correlation matrix. The two generally yield different PCs. Hence, just like PCA, we typically scale the variables to make their standard deviation one prior to performing cluster analysis, unless the application at hand suggests that certain variables should receive a higher weight.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.5"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-06","m":3,"t":"Q6.6 · PCA sign","q":"解释主成分的载荷（loadings）与得分（scores）\"在符号翻转的意义下唯一\"是何含义，以及为何会如此","h":"Explain why PC loadings and scores are unique only up to a sign flip.","a":"中文：若 \\phi_m 是第 m 个 PC 的一个载荷向量，则 -\\phi_m 也是。几何上：把 PC 载荷向量的符号取反，它所\"张成的直线\"不变（直线向两个方向延伸），因此仍是合法的 PC 方向。代数上：因为 \\mathrm{Var}(-Y)=\\mathrm{Var}(Y)，将所有载荷取反后样本方差仍为最大值；相应的 PC 得分向量 \\mathbf{z}_m 也同步变为 -\\mathbf{z}_m，故 PC 得分同样在符号翻转意义下唯一。\n\nEnglish: If \\phi_m is a loading vector of the mth PC, so is -\\phi_m. *Geometrically*: flipping the sign spans the same line (a line extends in both directions). *Algebraically*: \\mathrm{Var}(-Y)=\\mathrm{Var}(Y), so the flipped loadings achieve the same maximal variance. Consequently the corresponding score vector \\mathbf{z}_m is also unique only up to a sign flip.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.6"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-07","m":3,"t":"Q6.7 · PCA limits","q":"解释主成分分析的缺点（或局限性）","h":"Explain the disadvantages or limitations of PCA.","a":"中文：1. 可解释性差（Interpretability）：PCA 在 PA 考试中最大的缺点是，它可能不会产生可解释的结果。理解 PCs 的含义并不总是容易，因为 PCs 是原始特征的复杂线性组合。在 PA 考试项目中，客户通常关心影响目标变量的因素或从你工作中获得的可操作洞察，无法解释新生成的特征将是一个巨大的劣势。 2. 不适用于非线性关系（Not good for non-linear relationships）：PCA 本质上使用线性变换来总结和可视化高维数据集，其中变量是高度线性相关的。如果变量以非线性方式相关（例如多项式关系），那么 PCA 可能不是合适的工具。 3. 并非特征选择（PCA is not doing feature selection）：虽然 PCA 降低了模型的维度，但它并不是真正的特征选择方法。这是因为每个 PC 都是所有原始 p 个特征的线性组合，通常没有一个特征被移除。从实际角度来看，构建模型时仍然需要收集所有原始变量，因此 PCA 没有带来运营效率的提升。 4. 忽略目标变量（Target variable is ignored）：当我们在监督学习环境中使用 PCA 时，PC 载荷和得分完全独立于目标变量生成。我们隐含地假设特征表现出最大变异的方向（由载荷向量给出）也是与目标变量最相关的方向。通常没有保证这是真的。\n\nEnglish: 1. *Interpretability*: The greatest disadvantage of PCA in Exam PA is that it may not lead to interpretable results. It is not always an easy task to make sense of the PCs, which can be complicated linear combinations of the original features. The loss of interpretability is a particular concern in PA exam projects where your client is interested in factors affecting the target variable or actionable insights from your work. Not being able to interpret your newly generated features will be a huge downside. 2. *Not good for non-linear relationships*: By construction, PCA involves using linear transformations to summarize and visualize high-dimensional datasets where the variables are highly *linearly* correlated. If the variables are related in a non-linear fashion (e.g., polynomial relationships), then PCA may not be a good tool to use. 3. *PCA is not doing feature selection*: Although PCA reduces the dimensionality of the model, it is not exactly a feature selection method. This is because each PC is a linear combination of all of the original p features, none of which is removed in general. From a practical point of view, all of the original variables must still be collected for model construction, so no operational efficiency is achieved by PCA. 4. *Target variable is ignored*: When we use PCA in a supervised learning setting, the PC loadings and scores are generated completely independently of the target variable. We are implicitly assuming that the directions in which the features exhibit the most variation (given by the loading vectors) are also the directions most associated with the target variable. Often there is no guarantee that this is true.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.7"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-08","m":3,"t":"Q6.8 · K-means","q":"解释 K-means 聚类是如何工作的","h":"Explain how K-means clustering works.","a":"中文：K-means 聚类是一种直观简单、实现高效的聚类方法。对于该方法，我们必须预先指定簇的数量 K，目标是将每个观测分配到 K 个簇 C_1, C_2, \\dots, C_K 之一，每个簇包含相对同质的观测。同质性用簇内平方和（within-cluster SS） 量化：对于每个簇 C_k，其 within-cluster SS 定义为该簇中每个观测到其质心（centroid，即各特征均值的向量）的欧氏距离平方之和。K-means 的目标是最小化所有 K 个簇的 within-cluster SS 之和（总簇内 SS）。\n\nEnglish: K-means clustering is a clustering method that is intuitively simple to understand and practically efficient to implement. For this clustering method, we have to specify the number of clusters K upfront, and our objective is to assign each observation to one and only one of the K clusters, C_1, C_2, \\dots, C_K, each of which hosts relatively homogeneous observations. Homogeneity is quantified by the within-cluster sum of squares (SS) (a.k.a. within-cluster variation): for each cluster C_k, the within-cluster SS is defined as the sum of the squared Euclidean distances between each observation in C_k and the centroid (or center) of C_k. Using K-means clustering, we seek to identify the K clusters to minimize the total within-cluster SS.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.8"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-09","m":3,"t":"Q6.9 · K-means algorithm","q":"陈述 K-means 聚类算法","h":"State the K-means clustering algorithm.","a":"中文：Step 1: 初始化（Initialization）：在特征空间中随机选取 K 个点作为初始簇中心； Step 2: 迭代（Iteration）：重复以下步骤，直到簇分配不再变化： (a) 将每个观测分配给欧氏距离最近的中心所在的簇； (b) 重新计算（更新）每个簇的中心。 （注：欧氏距离要求特征为数值型，不能直接处理分类特征的原始形式。）\n\nEnglish: Step 1: Initialization: Randomly select K points in the feature space. These K points will serve as the initial cluster centers. Step 2: Iteration: Repeat the following steps until the cluster assignments no longer change: (a) Assign each observation to the cluster with the closest centroid (with respect to Euclidean distance). (b) Recalculate (update) the center of each of the K clusters. (Note: Euclidean distance requires that the features be numeric and cannot deal with categorical features in their raw form.)","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.9"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-10","m":3,"t":"Q6.10 · K-means name","q":"解释术语\"K-means\"指的是什么","h":"Explain what the term K-means means.","a":"中文：因为算法涉及反复重新计算 K 个均值（更准确地说是 K 个簇中心），这种聚类方法因此恰当地被称为 \"K-means\"（而不是\"K-cluster\"）聚类。\n\nEnglish: Because the algorithm involves iteratively recalculating the K means (more precisely, the K centers) of the clusters, such a clustering method is aptly called \"K-means\" (instead of \"K-cluster\") clustering.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.10"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-11","m":3,"t":"Q6.11 · K-means starts","q":"解释为何需要多次运行 K-means 聚类算法","h":"Explain why the K-means algorithm should be run multiple times.","a":"中文：尽管 K-means 简单高效，但该算法只能产生局部最优，而不一定是全局最优。\"局部最优\"意味着每次迭代都能保证降低总簇内 SS，算法终止时返回的簇分配在局部意义上是最优的——算法无法进一步降低总簇内 SS。然而，这组簇分配可能不是所有可能簇分组中最好的，即它可能不是全局最优。算法产生的局部最优严重依赖于随机的初始簇中心；不同的初始中心可能产生完全不同的最终簇集。对于某些数据集，离群点的存在也可能扭曲簇安排。为了减轻与初始簇中心相关的随机性，并增加识别全局最优和获得更具代表性簇组的机会，总是建议多次（如 20 到 50 次） 用不同的初始簇中心运行 K-means 算法，然后选择最佳解——即总簇内 SS 最低的簇分配。\n\nEnglish: Despite its simplicity and efficiency, the K-means clustering algorithm can only produce a local, but not necessarily a global optimum. \"Local optimum\" means that each iteration of the K-means clustering algorithm is guaranteed to reduce the total within-cluster SS. When the algorithm terminates, it returns a set of cluster assignments that are \"locally\" the best in the sense that the algorithm cannot reduce the total within-cluster SS any further. However, that set of cluster assignments may not be the best one of all possible cluster groupings, i.e., it may not be the global optimum. The local optimum produced by the algorithm relies heavily on the initial cluster centers, which are made randomly. A different set of initial cluster centers may give rise to an entirely different final set of clusters. For some datasets, the presence of outliers may also distort the cluster arrangements. To mitigate the randomness associated with the initial cluster centers and increase the chance of identifying a global optimum and getting more representative cluster groups, it is always advisable to run the K-means algorithm many times (e.g., 20 to 50) with different initial cluster centers. Then we select the best solution, i.e., the cluster assignments that result in the lowest total within-cluster SS.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.11"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-12","m":3,"t":"Q6.12 · Choose K","q":"解释肘部法（elbow method）如何用于选择 K 的取值","h":"Explain how the elbow method is used to select K.","a":"中文：与选择 PC 数量类似，选择 K 没有 universally accepted 的方法。肘部法是一种基于直观思想的图形工具：好的聚类分组具有较小的簇内 SS 和较大的簇间 SS。利用数学关系 \\text{Total SS} = \\text{Total within-cluster SS} + \\text{between-cluster SS}，其中 between-cluster SS 可被视为 K 个簇所解释的 SS。随着 K 增大，总簇内 SS 单调递减，簇间 SS 单调递增。我们对 K=1,2,\\dots 画出被解释方差比例 = between-cluster SS / Total SS 随 K 的变化曲线（elbow plot）。当被解释方差比例趋于平稳、即增加一个簇带来的边际增益开始下降时，我们说达到了一个\"elbow\"，对应的 K 即为合适的簇数。注意这是一种直观但主观的方法，没有唯一标准答案。\n\nEnglish: Very much like the choice of the number of PCs, there is no universally accepted way to select K. However, the elbow method is a graphical tool based on the intuitive idea that a good cluster grouping is characterized by a small within-cluster SS, but a large between-cluster SS, and the mathematical relationship: Total SS = Total within-cluster SS + between-cluster SS, where the between-cluster SS can be thought of as the SS explained by the K clusters. As K increases, the total within-cluster SS decreases monotonically while the between-cluster SS increases monotonically. We make an elbow plot showing the proportion of variation explained = between-cluster SS / Total SS for each value of K. When the proportion of variation explained has plateaued out, i.e., the marginal increase that comes with an additional cluster starts to drop off, we are said to have reached an \"elbow,\" and the corresponding value of K provides an appropriate number of clusters. The method is intuitive but subjective; no single number is uniquely correct.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.12"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-13","m":3,"t":"Q6.13 · Hierarchical clustering","q":"解释层次聚类是如何工作的","h":"Explain how hierarchical clustering works.","a":"中文：层次聚类（特别是 PA 关注的凝聚式/agglomerative 层次聚类）由一系列对数据中的观测进行融合（或合并） 组成。这种自底向上的聚类方法从单个观测开始，每个观测被视为一个单独的簇（\"singleton\" 簇），然后每次将距离最近的一对簇合并，一次一对。该过程反复进行，直到所有簇最终融合为一个包含所有观测的单一簇。簇之间的距离由连接方式（linkage） 定义：complete（最远点对距离）、single（最近点对距离）、average（所有点对距离的均值）、centroid（两簇质心之间的距离）。整个合并过程可由树状的 dendrogram（树状图） 可视化。无需预先指定 K——通过在 dendrogram 的合适高度进行\"横切\"即可得到所需簇数。\n\nEnglish: Agglomerative hierarchical clustering, or hierarchical clustering for short, consists of a series of fusions (or mergers) of observations in the data. This bottom-up clustering method starts with the individual observations, each treated as a separate cluster (a \"singleton\" cluster), and successively fuses the closest pair of clusters, one pair at a time. The process goes on iteratively until all clusters are eventually fused into a single cluster containing all of the observations. The distance between two clusters is determined by the linkage (complete, single, average, or centroid). The process can be visualized by a dendrogram, a tree-based visualization. The number of clusters K need not be specified in advance—it is chosen by cutting the dendrogram at a suitable height.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.13"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-14","m":3,"t":"Q6.14 · Linkage","q":"解释 average linkage 与 centroid linkage 之间的差异","h":"Explain the difference between average and centroid linkage.","a":"中文：Average linkage 和 centroid linkage 虽然表面相似，但在距离计算和取均值的顺序上不同： Average linkage：先计算两簇中所有观测之间的所有两两距离，再对这些距离取平均； Centroid linkage：先对两簇中各变量的特征值取平均得到两个簇的质心，再计算两个质心之间的距离。 由于计算顺序不同，average linkage 得到的距离一定不超过 centroid linkage 得到的距离。实践中，complete 和 average linkage 更常用，因为它们往往产生更均衡（簇内观测数相似）且视觉上更吸引人的簇。\n\nEnglish: Average linkage and centroid linkage, while similar on the surface, are different in terms of the order in which distance calculations and averaging are performed: For average linkage, we first compute all pairwise distances, then take an average. For centroid linkage, we first take an average of the feature values to get the two cluster centroids, then compute the distance between the two centroids. As a result, the average-linkage distance is not greater than the centroid-linkage distance. In practice, complete and average linkage are commonly used as they tend to result in more balanced (i.e., the clusters formed have a similar number of observations) and visually appealing clusters.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.14"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-15","m":3,"t":"Q6.15 · Clustering comparison","q":"解释 K-means 聚类与层次聚类之间的两点相同点与不同点","h":"Explain similarities and differences between K-means and hierarchical clustering.","a":"中文：相同点（Similarities）： 1. 两者都是无监督学习方法，没有目标变量（或即使有也被忽略）； 2. 两者的目标都是在观测中识别同质子群； 3. 两者对变量的缩放敏感——欧氏距离计算依赖于特征值的量纲； 4. 两者都对离群点敏感——聚类方法通常对数据的扰动不稳健，发现的簇可能被离群点严重扭曲。 不同点（Differences）： 1. 是否需要随机化：K-means 需要（用于创建初始簇中心），层次聚类不需要（总是产生相同的簇集，无随机性）； 2. 是否预先指定簇数：K-means 必须预先指定 K，层次聚类无需预先指定（K 可通过指定 dendrogram 的高度事后选择）； 3. 簇是否嵌套：K-means 的簇一般没有嵌套结构，层次聚类的簇具有嵌套结构（产生簇的层次结构）。\n\nEnglish: *Similarities*: 1. They are both unsupervised learning methods. There is no target variable, or it is ignored if present. 2. Objective: To uncover homogeneous subgroups among the observations. 3. Sensitive to scaling of variables? Yes — Euclidean distance calculations depend on the scale on which the feature values are measured. 4. Sensitive to outliers? Yes — clustering methods are generally non-robust to perturbations to the data, and clusters found may be heavily distorted by outliers. *Differences*: 1. Is randomization needed? K-means: Yes (needed for creating initial cluster centers). Hierarchical: No (same set of clusters is always created without randomness). 2. Is the number of clusters pre-specified? K-means: Yes (K has to be specified in advance). Hierarchical: No (K can be chosen later by specifying the height of the dendrogram). 3. Are the clusters nested? K-means: No (no nested structure in general). Hierarchical: Yes (a hierarchy of clusters).","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.15"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-16","m":3,"t":"Q6.16 · Clustering scaling","q":"解释对变量进行缩放会如何影响聚类的结果","h":"Explain how scaling variables affects clustering results.","a":"中文：对于 K-means 聚类和层次聚类，欧氏距离计算非常依赖于特征值测量的量纲。 不缩放（Without scaling）：如果变量不在同一单位且一个变量的数量级大得多，那么该变量将主导距离计算，对簇安排施加不成比例的影响。例如 X_1 从 0 到 1，X_2 从 0 到 1000，则任意一对观测之间的欧氏距离很大程度上归因于 X_2 的值，X_1 的值实际上无关紧要。 缩放（With scaling）：当特征被标准化后，我们在进行距离计算时本质上对每个特征赋予同等重要性，这对大多数应用来说更理想。 因此，与 PCA 类似，我们通常在聚类分析前将变量缩放到标准差为 1，除非应用场景暗示某些变量应获得更高权重。\n\nEnglish: For both K-means clustering and hierarchical clustering, the Euclidean distance calculations depend very much on the scale on which the feature values are measured. *Without scaling*: If the variables are not in the same unit and one variable is of a much larger order of magnitude, then that variable will dominate the distance calculations and exert a disproportionate impact on the cluster arrangements. For example, if X_1 ranges from 0 to 1 and X_2 ranges from 0 to 1000, then much of the Euclidean distance between any pair of observations is attributed to their X_2 values; their X_1 values do not really matter. *With scaling*: In contrast, when the features are standardized, we essentially attach equal importance to each feature when performing distance calculations, which is more desirable for most applications. Hence, just like PCA, we typically scale the variables to make their standard deviation one prior to performing cluster analysis, unless the application at hand suggests that certain variables should receive a higher weight.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.16"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-17","m":3,"t":"Q6.17 · Cluster features","q":"解释聚类可用于为预测目标变量生成特征的两个方式","h":"Explain two ways clustering can create features for predicting a target.","a":"中文：1. 簇分组（Cluster groups）：聚类产生的分组分配是一个因子变量，可以替代原始变量使用，作为预测目标变量的潜在有用特征。这种简单的特征生成方法曾在一些过去的 PA 考试项目中测试过，例如 2020 年 12 月 7 日考试的 Task 5。 2. 簇中心（Cluster centers）：不用簇分组作为因子特征，而是将原始变量替换为簇中心，作为新的数值型特征。这种方法的优势在于： 可解释性：簇中心提供了不同簇中观测特征的数值摘要，通过检查簇中心，我们可能能够判断聚类捕捉了数据的哪些方面； 预测性：通过簇中心，这种方法保留了观测的数值特征，并使用汇总特征来帮助做出更好的预测。相比之下，如果使用簇分组，数值特征将全部丢失。\n\nEnglish: 1. *Cluster groups*: The group assignments created as a result of clustering is a factor variable which may be used in place of the original variables and serve as a potentially useful feature for predicting a target variable. This simple feature generation method was tested in some past PA exam projects, e.g., Task 5 of the December 7, 2020 exam. 2. *Cluster centers*: Instead of using the cluster groups as a factor feature, we may replace the original variables by the cluster centers, which will serve as new numeric features. This alternative feature generation method has the following advantages: *Interpretation*: The cluster centers provide a numeric summary of the characteristics of the observations in different clusters. Examining the cluster centers, we may be able to tell what aspects of the data are captured by the clusters. *Prediction*: Via the cluster centers, this method retains the numeric characteristics of the observations and uses the summarized characteristics to help make better predictions. In contrast, the numeric characteristics will be all gone if the cluster groups are used.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.17"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-18","m":3,"t":"Q6.18 · High dimensions","q":"解释为何在高维情境下聚类分析的效果会下降（给出两点理由）","h":"Explain two reasons clustering becomes less effective in high dimensions.","a":"中文：1. 可视化困难：当 p=2 时，我们可以用二维散点图展示聚类分配。当 p \\ge 3 时，可视化变得困难得多。（一种解决方案是用 PCA 将数据压缩到二维，然后显示由簇分组标识的 PC 得分。） 2. \"近\"与\"远\"变得难以区分：随着维数增加，我们的直觉失效，区分哪些观测近、哪些观测远变得更加困难。例如，在 p=100 维中，\\mathbf{x}_1=(0,0,\\dots,0)、\\mathbf{x}_2=(1,1,\\dots,1)、\\mathbf{x}_3=(0,0,\\dots,0,10)，则 d(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\mathbf{x}_2)=\\sqrt{100}=10，d(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\mathbf{x}_3)=\\sqrt{10^2}=10。观测 2 和 3 与观测 1 等距，尽管它们看起来是相当不同的观测。由于聚类依赖于某些观测比其他观测更近（因此被合并到同一簇）这一事实，而\"近\"的概念在变量越来越多时变得更加模糊，聚类在高维情况下变得不那么有效。这就是维度灾难（curse of dimensionality）。\n\nEnglish: 1. *Visualization of the results becomes problematic*: With p=2 variables, we can use a two-dimensional scatterplot to display the cluster assignments. When p is larger than or equal to 3, visualization is much harder. (A solution is to compress the data into two dimensions using PCA, and display the PC scores identified by the cluster groups.) 2. *Notions of \"close\" and \"far\" break down*: As the number of dimensions increases, our intuition breaks down and it becomes harder to differentiate between observations that are close and those that are far apart. For instance, in p=100 dimensions, \\mathbf{x}_1=(0,0,\\dots,0), \\mathbf{x}_2=(1,1,\\dots,1), \\mathbf{x}_3=(0,0,\\dots,0,10). Then d(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\mathbf{x}_2)=\\sqrt{100}=10 and d(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\mathbf{x}_3)=\\sqrt{10^2}=10. Observations 2 and 3 are equidistant from observation 1, even though they appear to be quite different observations. As clustering relies on the fact that some observations are closer to each other (hence combined into the same cluster) than others, and the notion of closeness becomes more fuzzy when there are more and more variables, clustering becomes less effective in high dimensions. This is the curse of dimensionality.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.18"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"},{"id":"cq6-19","m":3,"t":"Q6.19 · PCA before clustering","q":"解释主成分分析如何能作为在对高维数据集应用聚类之前的预处理步骤","h":"Explain how PCA can be used before clustering a high-dimensional dataset.","a":"中文：先用 PCA 把 p 个原始变量压缩为少数几个保留大部分方差（例如前两个）的主成分，得到每条观测的 PC 得分；然后在低维 PC 空间上运行 K-means 或层次聚类。这样做有两个好处：① 距离计算和聚类运算在低维空间更稳定、更快；② 由于保留了大部分信息，聚类结果本质上与在全特征空间聚类接近，但又能直接用前两个 PC 做二维散点图来直观地展示和诊断聚类结果。\n\nEnglish: First apply PCA to compress the p original variables into a small number of PCs (e.g., the first two) that retain most of the variance, then run K-means or hierarchical clustering on the PC scores. This (1) makes distance calculations and clustering faster/more stable in the lower-dimensional space, and (2) allows the resulting clusters to be visualized in a 2D scatterplot of PC1 vs PC2 while preserving most of the information in the original data.","k":["Chapter 6","conceptual review","Q6.19"],"hi":0,"kind":"concept"}];
